<title>TURKEY: Turkey's main 1997 economic, budgetary targets.</title>
<headline>Turkey's main 1997 economic, budgetary targets.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish Finance Minister Abdullatif Sener announced on Friday the following figures as the country's main 1997 economic and budgetary targets.</p>
<p>    GNP (Gross National Product)     : 25,360 trillion lira</p>
<p>						   ($187.85 billion)</p>
<p>    GNP growth rate			:  4 percent</p>
<p>    GNP deflator			   : 65 percent</p>
<p>    Exports				  : $29.5 billion</p>
<p>    Imports				  : $50 billion</p>
<p>    Foreign trade deficit		: $20.5 billion</p>
<p>    Current account deficit	    : $5.6 billion</p>
<p>    Year-on-year wholesale inflation : 57.7 percent</p>
<p>    Average yearly inflation	   : 65 percent</p>
<p>    Average yearly dollar rate	 : 135,000 lira</p>
<p>    Consolidated budget revenues     : 6,255 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Taxes				  : 4,368 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Non-tax incl. privatisation    : 1,445 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Funds				  :   425 trillion lira</p>
<p>	State enterprises		  :    17 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Consolidated budget expenditures : 6,255 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Personnel			    : 1,675 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Other current spending	   :   669.8 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Investments			  :   524.6 trillion lira</p>
<p>	Transfers incl. intr. payments : 3,385.6 trillon lira</p>
<p>    Consolidated budget deficit	: 0</p>
<p>	    -- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 0875. EKS</p>
</text>
